    "## Task 3: Text Vectorization\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why must text be converted to numbers?**  \n",
    "Machine learning models and neural networks only understand numbers — they cannot process raw text. Vectorization converts each word/sentence into a numerical representation that models can compute on.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Three methods used:**\n",
    "\n",
    "| Method | How It Works | Best For |\n",
    "|--------|-------------|---------|\n",
    "| **Bag of Words (BoW)** | Counts how many times each word appears | Simple, fast models |\n",
    "| **TF-IDF** | Weighs words by importance (rare = more important) | Traditional ML |\n",
    "| **Tokenizer + Padding** | Converts words to integer IDs, keeps order | Deep learning (LSTM) |\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "03b1cd94",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Label Encoding: {'negative': np.int64(0), 'neutral': np.int64(1), 'positive': np.int64(2)}\n",
      "\n",
      "Train set: 1200 records\n",
      "Test set : 300 records\n",
      "\n",
      "BoW matrix shape: (1200, 148)\n",
      "  Each row = 1 message, each column = 1 unique word\n",
      "  Value = count of that word in the message\n",
      "\n",
      "TF-IDF matrix shape: (1200, 426)\n",
      "  ngram_range=(1,2) means single words AND word pairs are features\n",
      "\n",
      "Tokenized sequence shape: (1200, 30)\n",
