   "source": [
    "## Task 5: LSTM Sequence Model\n",
    "\n",
    "### Architecture Design\n",
    "\n",
    "Unlike traditional ML models (Naive Bayes, Logistic Regression) that ignore word order, **LSTM** (Long Short-Term Memory) reads text **word by word in sequence** — just like a human reads a sentence. This allows it to understand context.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Layer | Role |\n",
    "|-------|------|\n",
    "| **Embedding** | Converts each word ID into a 64-dimensional vector — words with similar meaning get similar vectors |\n",
    "| **LSTM(64)** | Reads the sequence word by word, remembers important context using memory cells |\n",
    "| **Dropout(0.4)** | Randomly turns off 40% of neurons during training — prevents overfitting |\n",
    "| **Dense(32, ReLU)** | Learns non-linear combinations of LSTM output features |\n",
    "| **Dense(3, Softmax)** | Outputs probability for each of 3 classes (positive/negative/neutral) |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Loss Function:** Sparse Categorical Crossentropy (standard for multi-class classification)  \n",
    "**Optimizer:** Adam (adaptive learning rate — works well for NLP)  \n",
    "**Evaluation Metric:** Accuracy\n"
   ]
  },
